Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::a_name_always_decodes_into_its_documented_buffer`.

The defect: the label is measured against half the buffer, as if two bytes of UTF-8 sufficed for
each UTF-16 code unit. A label of 36 three-byte characters (any CJK name) needs 108 bytes and is
refused from the documented 144-byte buffer.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(written.is_ok())`, on any name whose UTF-8 form passes 72
bytes.
diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs
index 9aff667e7..9a15a97ad 100644
--- a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs
+++ b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs
@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@ impl Entry {
         for ch in char::decode_utf16(self.name[..units].iter().copied()) {
             let ch = ch.unwrap_or(char::REPLACEMENT_CHARACTER);
             let len = ch.len_utf8();
-            if written + len > out.len() {
+            if written + len > out.len() / 2 {
                 return Err(Error::NameTooLong);
             }
             ch.encode_utf8(&mut out[written..]);
